exports[`export_draft_docx > refuses on an open Inventor Question and on claims changed after approval 1`] = `
{
  "claimsChanged": "The draft was not exported. drafting/hinge/claims.md changed after it was approved, so \`approved\` was set to \`false\`. The attorney reviews the claims and sets \`approved: true\` again; then start_application_draft and a new save start the next draft version.",
  "openQuestionRefusal": "The draft was not exported. 1 finding(s) in drafting/hinge/findings.md are open. Each Error and Inventor Question is resolved in the draft, or the attorney waives it with a reason (\`  - Waived: <reason>\` under the item):
- \`inventor-question\` (draft-application.md, line 41): Inventor Question IQ-1 is open: Which steel grade is the lever made of?",
  "unapproved": "The draft was not exported. \`approved\` in drafting/hinge/claims.md is not \`true\`. The attorney sets \`approved: true\` after review; a statement in chat does not open this gate.",
}
`;

exports[`start_application_draft > returns the inputs and the style exemplars, labelled style only, and records the approved claims 1`] = `
{
  "pdfReads": [
    "/workspace/style/c.pdf",
  ],
  "record": "# Working record — hinge

Companion to [draft-application.md](draft-application.md): how this Draft Application was made. Internal; not part of the filed application.

## Header

- **Approved claims SHA-256:** <sha>
",
  "result": "Drafting started for matter "hinge". Office: US. Gates read from the files: \`confirmed: true\` in drafting/hinge/feature-list.md, \`approved: true\` in drafting/hinge/claims.md. The approved claims are recorded (SHA-256 <sha>) in drafting/hinge/draft-application.working-record.md: when drafting/hinge/claims.md changes, the drafting tools set \`approved\` to \`false\` and refuse until the attorney approves again.
Save the draft with write_patent_results, template draft-application, to drafting/hinge/draft-application.md; then call validate_draft.

## Feature List (drafting/hinge/feature-list.md)

| ID | Feature | Source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| F1 | A housing 12 that holds a lever 14 of steel. | disclosure:§1 |

## Figures (drafting/hinge/figures.md)

## FIG. 1

- 12: housing
- 14: lever

## Approved Claims (drafting/hinge/claims.md)

1. A hinge comprising a housing and a lever.
2. The hinge of claim 1, wherein the lever is steel.

## Style exemplars (style only, never a source)

Voice and structure only. No fact, feature, embodiment, value, example or result enters the draft from an exemplar.

### Style exemplar 1: style/a.md (style only, never a source)

In one embodiment, the widget turns.

### Style exemplar 2: style/b.docx (style only, never a source)

The present disclosure relates to doors.

### Style exemplar 3: style/c.pdf (style only, never a source)

Text of the PDF exemplar.",
}
`;

exports[`validate_draft > keeps the attorney's waiver across two runs and merges the advisory items 1`] = `
{
  "findings": "# Findings

Errors and Inventor Questions block export until they are resolved or waived. To waive one, add a line \`  - Waived: <reason>\` under it. Notes never block. Advisory items come from the model review; they are advice, not a pass.

## Errors

None.

## Inventor Questions

- \`inventor-question\` (draft-application.md, line 41): Inventor Question IQ-1 is open: Which steel grade is the lever made of?
  - Waived: Grade is left to the manufacturer.

## Notes

None.

## Advisory

- \`advisory\` (draft-application.md, line 27, claim 2): Claim 2: "steel" has literal basis, but no passage supports steel in combination with the housing.
",
  "second": "Wrote drafting/hinge/findings.md (US validators, 1 advisory item(s); waivers kept).
Errors: 0 (0 waived). Inventor Questions: 1 (1 waived). Notes: 0. Advisory: 1.
No unwaived Error and no open Inventor Question.
Report these by severity with their line references. Do not call the draft passed or ready to file.",
}
`;

exports[`write_patent_results draft-application template > starts the next version when the claims changed and were approved again, keeping the previous draft and record 1`] = `
{
  "cleared": "Drafting did not start. drafting/hinge/claims.md changed after it was approved, so \`approved\` was set to \`false\`. The attorney reviews the claims and sets \`approved: true\` again; then start_application_draft and a new save start the next draft version.",
  "previousDraftVersion": "1",
  "previousRecordKept": true,
  "result": "Saved drafting/hinge/draft-application.md (version 2, office US). Generated snapshot: drafting/hinge/draft-application.generated.md. Working record: drafting/hinge/draft-application.working-record.md.
The claims changed since version 1: this is version 2; the previous files are kept as drafting/hinge/draft-application.v1.md, drafting/hinge/draft-application.v1.generated.md, drafting/hinge/draft-application.v1.working-record.md.
Findings are not checked at save. Call validate_draft next.",
  "version": "2",
}
`;

